# The build context for defense/Dockerfile is this directory, not defense/,
# because that image compiles two module trees: defense imports the bus envelope
# and the broker from queue through a replace directive, and Docker cannot COPY
# from outside its context.
#
# Without this file that context is the whole monorepo -- node_modules alone is
# hundreds of megabytes -- uploaded to the daemon on every build and then almost
# entirely ignored. api/ and ai/ already learned this lesson in their own
# .dockerignore files; ai/'s context was 59 MB, 57 MB of it a host-built venv.
#
# An ALLOWLIST rather than a deny list, for the same reason queue/.dockerignore
# is one: a new top-level directory should not silently join every build context.
#
# The other services are unaffected. Compose gives api, ai, web and queue their
# own context (`build: ./api`), so this file applies only to the root-context
# build.
*

!defense/go.mod
!defense/go.sum
!defense/binding/
!defense/internal/
!defense/cmd/

!queue/go.mod
!queue/go.sum
!queue/bus/
!queue/broker/

# data/ builds from this context too, and it is the one image that needs a file
# from a SIBLING service: api/src/ontologia.json, the generated ontology
# artefact. It is baked into the image rather than mounted so that the running
# service checks against the same bytes the build proved.
!data/go.mod
!data/go.sum
!data/internal/
!data/cmd/
!api/src/ontologia.json

# api now imports the sole auth implementation from the sibling /auth folder,
# so its Docker build also uses the root context.
!package.json
!api/package.json
!api/pnpm-lock.yaml
!api/tsconfig.json
!api/prisma.config.ts
!api/prisma/
!api/src/
!auth/

# Never, under any allowlist. Listed explicitly because a future `!something`
# broad enough to catch them would be a secret baked into an image layer, which
# survives deletion of the file.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
